Author: ModFii Remediation Agent <agent@modfii.local>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 16:25:36 2026 +0000

    fix(markdown): render H4+ headings and guarantee parser progress
    
    Root cause of the 2026-09-11 production outage: a line starting with
    '#### ' fell through to the paragraph block, whose inner loop breaks on
    any '#' line WITHOUT consuming it. The outer loop re-examined the same
    line forever, allocating React elements until the Node heap (2GB) died —
    one GET to an affected /learn/* article OOM-crashed next-server and the
    origin served 502 for every route.
    
    - add explicit '#### ' branch rendering an h4
    - paragraph branch now always consumes >= 1 line (loop-safety guard)
    - regression: src/lib/markdown.test.ts (heading levels, loop safety,
      full-corpus render, both affected articles)

